jobs.description:
As a Production Employee at Bavaria in Lieshout, you will play an important role in brewing and packaging one of the Netherlands' most iconic beers. In our state-of-the-art bottling facility, you help fill approximately 100,000 cans and bottles every hour.

Working at Bavaria means being involved in the entire production process. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that production runs as smoothly and efficiently as possible. Your shift starts and ends with a handover, where you discuss production results, breakdowns, and other important details with operators from the other teams.

At Bavaria, you will enjoy a varied role with responsibilities including:

- Setting up and adjusting machines;
- Troubleshooting common technical issues;
- Performing maintenance on the production line;
- Sorting returnable bottles;
- Supplying packaging machines with caps and rolls;
- Monitoring and checking beer quality.

Working Hours & Availability

Until January, you will work in a fixed 3-shift rotation with a repeating three-week cycle:

- Week 1: 4 to 5 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- Week 2: 3 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM and 2 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- Week 3: 3 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM and 2 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM

From January onwards, you will transition to a fixed 5-shift rotation schedule:

- 2 early shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- 2 late shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM
- 2 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- 4 days off

Are you ready to become part of this dynamic family-owned company? Apply now and you could soon be working in the bottling facility of Royal Swinkels!

- You are available to work in a 5-shift rotation schedule and till januari in a 3-shift schedule; 
- You have a good command of either the Dutch or English language;
- You are eager to learn and develop new skills.

- Packing and repacking products into cardboard export boxes;
- Preparing creams in a 400-liter mixing tank according to established formulas;
- Operating filling machines for tubes, wound care products, and FFP2 face masks;
- Replenishing raw materials and production supplies;
- Accurately completing production and quality documentation;
- Identifying and resolving minor technical issues;
- Setting up and changing over production lines;
- Supporting warehouse operations when needed;
- Working in accordance with CE, FDA, and cleanroom guidelines;
- Contributing ideas for process improvements and preventing recurring technical issues.

The company places a strong emphasis on independence. You will be trained to operate multiple machines and production stations independently as part of your development within the organization.

- Holds at least a VAPRO A diploma or an equivalent qualification;
- Speaks and writes either Dutch or English;
- Has technical insight and can analyze and solve equipment malfunctions;
- Works accurately, takes responsibility, and can work independently;
- Feels comfortable in an environment where quality standards and procedures are important;
- Brings discipline, energy, and a positive attitude to work.

Are you looking for a fun day-shift position in production where no two days are the same? Then keep reading!

For one of our clients in Lomm, we are looking for a motivated Production Employee. Your main responsibilities will include assembly work and supporting the blister packaging process of products.

Our client manufactures high-quality door hardware. To improve quality, durability, and weather resistance, the components are treated with a special coating.

In addition to assembly tasks, you may also be assigned to other departments, such as:

- Powder Coating: treating and finishing components;
- Assembly: assembling the door fittings for packaging;
- Sawing: cutting profiles to the correct dimensions;
- Packing: packaging finished products.

This is a day-shift position from 7:30 AM to 4:15 PM. You will work in a varied environment with the prospect of a long-term collaboration. Overtime may be required occasionally, always in consultation.

- You are available full-time for day-shift work and are looking for a serious, long-term job;
- You preferably speak Dutch, or alternatively are fluent in English or German;
- You do not mind performing repetitive tasks;
- The work can be physically demanding due to prolonged standing and handling/positioning products, so you should be comfortable with physical work.

As an Order Picker, you help make sure customers receive their orders quickly and correctly.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Packing and preparing orders for shipment;
- Placing products in the correct warehouse locations;
- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Helping colleagues when needed;
- Keeping the warehouse clean and safe.

Working Hours

You will work 40 hours per week.

You can choose between:

Morning Shift

- 07:00 AM to 04:00 PM

Evening Shift

- 04:00 PM to 01:00 AM

- MBO level or similar working and thinking level;
- Motivated and willing to work hard;
- Accurate and reliable;
- Able to speak Dutch or English;
- Physically fit and comfortable with warehouse work;
- Own transportation (car, scooter, moped, or e-bike);
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.
